meta {
  name: 01 Capability Statement
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/metadata
  body: none
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Accept: application/fhir+json
}

docs {
  # What the server advertises about itself

  `GET [base]/metadata` returns a **CapabilityStatement** — the machine-readable
  contract for this server:

  - `fhirVersion` — which FHIR version (expect `4.0.1` for R4).
  - `software.name` / `software.version` — e.g. HAPI FHIR 7.x.
  - `rest[0].resource[]` — every resource type and, per type, which
    `interaction`s (read / vread / update / create / search-type / history) and
    which `searchParam`s it supports.
  - `rest[0].interaction[]` — system-level interactions (transaction, batch,
    search-system, history-system).

  Read this first for ANY server before writing a client — it tells you what is
  and is not allowed.
}
